      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The added locals scan addresses direct local references, but its line-based block extraction can still miss a credential assignment later in a locals block. An output can then expose that opaque value without failing the test.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/release-identity.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 423,
          "message": "The locals-block scan can truncate before a credential-bearing assignment when a nested object closes at column zero. Parse the full block or otherwise ensure an output referencing that local fails AC RELEASE-ID-04.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The assertion extracts each output or locals block only through the first line beginning with `}`. If a locals block contains a multiline object whose closing brace begins at column zero, the match ends before later local assignments. The evaluated-output check can miss opaque credential values.",
            "failureScenario": "If a locals block puts a multiline object first and then assigns `hidden_key = azurerm_storage_account.demo.primary_access_key`, with the object’s closing brace at column zero, the regex stops before `hidden_key`. An output changed to `local.hidden_key` contains no credential attribute in its source, and the resulting opaque key may match none of the evaluated-value patterns. The test can pass while an output exposes storage-key material, contrary to AC RELEASE-ID-04 (OWASP A02:2025 Security Misconfiguration)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
